[{"role": "user", "content": "I'm trying to make a chocolate soufflé recipe I found online, but it's written for a European audience using metric measurements. It says to preheat the oven to 180°C, requires 200g of dark chocolate and 150ml of heavy cream. My American oven displays Fahrenheit, and all my measuring cups and kitchen scale use ounces and cups. Can you help me convert all these measurements so I can make this recipe with my current kitchen setup?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll help you convert all those metric measurements to US customary units so you can make your chocolate soufflé! Let me convert each one for you."}, {"role": "tool_call", "content": "{'name': 'cooking-units-converter-convert_temperature', 'arguments': '{"value": 180, "from_unit": "C", "to_unit": "F"}'}"}, {"role": "tool_call", "content": "{'name': 'cooking-units-converter-convert_weight', 'arguments': '{"value": 200, "from_unit": "g", "to_unit": "oz"}'}"}, {"role": "tool_call", "content": "{'name': 'cooking-units-converter-convert_volume', 'arguments': '{"value": 150, "from_unit": "ml", "to_unit": "cup"}'}"}, {"role": "tool_response", "content": "{
  "value": 356.0,
  "from_unit": "C",
  "to_unit": "F"
}"}, {"role": "tool_response", "content": "{
  "value": 7.0548,
  "from_unit": "g",
  "to_unit": "oz"
}"}, {"role": "tool_response", "content": "{
  "value": 0.634,
  "from_unit": "ml",
  "to_unit": "cup"
}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect! Here are all your converted measurements for the chocolate soufflé recipe:

- **Oven temperature**: 180°C = **356°F** (you can round this to **350°F** for most ovens)
- **Dark chocolate**: 200g = **7.05 ounces** (approximately **7 ounces**)
- **Heavy cream**: 150ml = **0.634 cups** (approximately **2/3 cup**)

Now you're all set to make your chocolate soufflé with your American kitchen setup! Most measuring cups have 2/3 cup markings, and 7 ounces is a common chocolate bar size, so these should be easy to measure."}]

